---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import VmCostComparator from '../../components/VmCostComparator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Cloud VM Cost Comparator (AWS / Azure / GCP)" description="Compare monthly cost across similar-spec VMs on AWS, Azure, and GCP.">
  <VmCostComparator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why compare across providers</h2>
  <p>Similarly-specced instances can differ meaningfully in price between providers. This gives a quick directional comparison before you commit — always verify current pricing for your specific region before budgeting.</p>

  <h2>Common VM Cost Comparison Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Comparing list prices without considering committed-use discounts</strong> — reserved instances or committed-use plans can shift the real cost picture significantly.</li>
    <li><strong>Ignoring regional price variation</strong> — the same instance type can cost differently across regions within the same provider.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This VM Cost Comparator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Getting a directional cost comparison before choosing a cloud provider</li>
    <li>Estimating infrastructure budget for a new project</li>
    <li>Comparing similarly-specced instances across providers for a migration decision</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
